==English==
{{wp}}

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|fr|en}} {{m|fr|cilice}}, from {{etyl|la|en}} {{m|la|cilicium||clothing made of [[goatskin]]}}, from {{m|la|Cilicia}} where it originates from.

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# A [[garment]] or [[undergarment]] made of coarse cloth or animal hair worn close to the skin used by members of various Christian traditions as a self-imposed means of [[penance]] ([[repentance]]) and [[mortification]] of the flesh.
# {{lb|en|chiefly|in Opus Dei}} A [[leather]] [[strap]] [[stud]]ded with [[metallic]] [[barb]]s that cut into [[flesh]] as a constant [[reminder]] of [[Christ]]'s [[suffering]].

====Synonyms====
* {{l|en|sackcloth}}
* {{l|en|hairshirt}}

====Derived terms====
* {{l|en|chain cilice}}
* {{l|en|hairshirt cilice}}

